    // latest after capMs. It replaces fixed "let the render settle" sleeps: the cap is the old sleep, so it never waits longer
    // than before, and it returns early once React has committed and nothing else is changing. NOT for sleeps that prove
    // that nothing happened (a click-defer or debounce timer, a "nothing was written" window): those wait on a timer the DOM
